.TH HTTP_READ_INTERNAL 3
.SH NAME
http_read_internal \- decode the input buffer of an HTTP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_read_internal(fd_type " fd ", char * " buf ", size_t " len ", buffer* " b ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_read_internal ()
does the work of
.BR http_read (3)
on what is in the input buffer
.IR h->q.in :
in the state HTTP_RECV_HEADER it reads the headers with
.BR http_read_header (3),
in HTTP_RECV_DATA it copies as much body data as is available and allowed by
.BR http_response_read (3)
into
.IR buf .
.P
This belongs to the first reader of the module, written for
.BR buffer (3)
operations; it expects
.I h->stream
to be cleared. New code should use
.BR http_recv (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of body bytes copied, 0 if there are none, -1 if the response is in the state HTTP_STATUS_ERROR.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_read(3), http_response_read(3)
